 <metadata name="Description">&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;Toy story inspired dumplings- prints in place.&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&amp;amp;nbsp;&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;Logo can be shaped in a curve right off of the hot plate.  If it has cooled already, you can use heat of your choice to warm it up and curve it.&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&amp;amp;nbsp;&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;Adding logo to the dumpling container.&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;&amp;lt;span style=&amp;#34;background-color: rgb(255,255,255)&amp;#34;&amp;gt;Step 1: Print the Parts Print all required 3D parts. Ensure surfaces are clean and dry before applying the logo. &amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;span style=&amp;#34;background-color: rgb(255,255,255)&amp;#34;&amp;gt;Step 2: Apply Glue to the logo Place the label face down. Apply a thin, even layer of E6000 glue to the back of the logo. Avoid excess glue near the edges. &amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;span style=&amp;#34;background-color: rgb(255,255,255)&amp;#34;&amp;gt;Step 3: Position the logo in the desired area. Press gently to ensure full contact. &amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;span style=&amp;#34;background-color: rgb(255,255,255)&amp;#34;&amp;gt;Step 4: Secure the logo with a rubber band or painter’s tape to hold it in place while drying. &amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&amp;amp;nbsp;&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;span style=&amp;#34;background-color: rgb(255,255,255)&amp;#34;&amp;gt;Allow it to dry completely, preferably overnight&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br&amp;gt; &amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;</metadata>
